# Feed packages that need OpenWrt development dependencies staged while
# compiling. This includes ports, OpenWrt-derived binaries and AudioWRT native C
# packages that include/link against OpenWrt feed libraries.
#
# Packages NOT listed here stay on the NO_DEPS=1 package boundary. Runtime-only
# OpenWrt dependencies must never turn into source-build roots.
#
# Wi-Fi ownership:
# - hostapd-wpa-supplicant-tailored compiles one multicall
#   hostapd+wpa_supplicant binary from the exact OpenWrt hostap source, but stays
#   on the NO_DEPS=1 boundary. scripts/build.sh stages only its required
#   development interfaces from exact-release sources/APKs.
#
# Bluetooth ownership:
# - bluez-trimmed builds only the constrained bluetoothd daemon; runtime
#   libbluetooth comes from the official OpenWrt bluez-libs package.
# - bluez-trimmed, audiowrt-btctl and bluez-alsa compile against the official
#   OpenWrt glib2 development interface through PKG_BUILD_DEPENDS, while their
#   firmware runtime dependency is glib2-trimmed.
# - audiowrt-btctl is AudioWRT-owned C code but needs GLib/GIO development
#   headers, so it uses the explicit development-dependency path.
# - bluez-alsa is a port from official upstream source and uses the selected
#   OpenWrt development interfaces.

librespot
bluez-trimmed
audiowrt-btctl
bluez-alsa
